MID_EV14_004_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_004_m01_001: Sirocco, I've been wondering. What is Kassite like?
MID_EV14_004_m01_002: Let's see. It's the capital of Cydonia and built in the\nmountains. And if memory serves, it's not very big.
MID_EV14_004_m01_003: It used to be the sort of town a bard like myself\nwouldn't find very interesting.
MID_EV14_004_m01_004: Do you find it interesting now?
MID_EV14_004_m01_005: Well, tragedy struck there four years ago. Some call it\nthe Siege of Cydonia, others the Cydonia Massacre.
MID_EV14_004_m01_006: Is it interesting? Indeed. But that wound is still\nfresh, so I won't be writing any songs about it.
MID_EV14_004_m01_007: I've never heard of that...massacre. What happened?
MID_EV14_004_m01_008: Soldiers from the kingdom of Arago descended upon\nKassite, which was then part of the Dagdan Empire.
MID_EV14_004_m01_009: It's said they poured over the walls and into the city,\nkilling many people—the viceroy included.
MID_EV14_004_m01_010: That's when the Dagdan Empire transferred control\nof Cydonia to Arago.
MID_EV14_004_m01_011: The Dagdan Empire abandoned Cydonia. Cut it off\nand threw it away.
MID_EV14_004_m01_012: Kassite was a simple place...peaceful. It had little in\nthe way of wealth or extravagance.
MID_EV14_004_m01_013: But it was a beautiful town where good people led\nhappy lives.
MID_EV14_004_m01_014: Ah, it sounds like you know the area well.
MID_EV14_004_m01_015: Lady Leda and I used to live there. But we haven't\nvisited since...that time.
MID_EV14_004_m01_016: It must look very different now.
MID_EV14_004_m01_017: The people who would remember what kind of place\nit was have likely scattered.
MID_EV14_004_m01_018: Indeed. From what I've heard, it never recovered\nfrom the invasion and remains in ruins even now.
MID_EV14_004_m01_019: Tch...
MID_EV14_004_m01_020: Bjor said he sent my mother to someone named\nBalboa. Doesn't she live there?
MID_EV14_004_m01_021: It would seem so. After serving as general of Arago's\narmy, she took a post as Cydonia's viceroy.
MID_EV14_004_m01_022: One does not hear good things about her. It's said she\nenjoys keeping the region under the heel of her boot.
MID_EV14_004_m01_023: It was Balboa who commanded the invasion\nof Cydonia.
MID_EV14_004_m01_024: And after the battle, she pinned the blame for\neverything on the previous viceroy.
MID_EV14_004_m01_025: As if that weren't enough, she ordered her soldiers to\nloot Kassite, bringing death and misery to so many.
MID_EV14_004_m01_026: But she won't get away with it. I will hunt her down,\nand I will kill her.
MID_EV14_004_m01_027: I do wish I understood how you arrived at such an\nextreme loathing for that lot.
MID_EV14_004_m01_028: Ah well, I've decided to follow you on this quest of\nyours. What can I say? I find you fascinating. 
MID_EV14_004_m01_029: And I have a feeling something interesting awaits us\nin Kassite.
MID_EV14_005_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_005_m01_001: Mu, I have to ask. Why do you wear clothes like\nthat? They make you look like a boy.
MID_EV14_005_m01_002: What do you mean?! I am a boy! I mean a man!\nUh... Why are you so stupid and weird, huh?!
MID_EV14_005_m01_003: Listen to me, Mu. Girls start to look more feminine\naround your age.
MID_EV14_005_m01_004: And at my age, it's easy to spot, no matter what kind\nof attire...or persona...one tries to hide behind.
MID_EV14_005_m01_005: And let's not forget how upset you got when\nI approached you during that dustup with Bjor.
MID_EV14_005_m01_006: Disgusting pig! Don't look at me like that!
MID_EV14_005_m01_007: Mu?! You're a... I-I didn't know!
MID_EV14_005_m01_008: Buccar! You really couldn't tell?
MID_EV14_005_m01_009: I assure you, Mu, I am not looking at you in any\nsuch way. I prefer older women.
MID_EV14_005_m01_010: You have nothing to worry about, I promise.
MID_EV14_005_m01_011: <NCA>Ask Mu about her situation.
MID_EV14_005_m01_012: Hm. What's your story anyway, Mu? And why are\nyou pretending to be a boy?
MID_EV14_005_m01_013: Well, after my mother left home to find work,\nmy auntie took me in.
MID_EV14_005_m01_014: She's my mom's big sister. She took really good\ncare of me.
MID_EV14_005_m01_015: And my mom sent me letters for the first few months\nafter she left. But then they just...stopped.
MID_EV14_005_m01_016: My auntie didn't want me to go looking for her.\nBut I was worried. So, I ran away.
MID_EV14_005_m01_017: Everyone always says it's dangerous for a girl to\ntravel alone, so I dressed like this.
MID_EV14_005_m01_018: They're not wrong. There are plenty of dangerous\npeople out there who do bad things to women.
MID_EV14_005_m01_019: Don't look at me! And as long as we're discussing\nidentities, real or otherwise, I'm curious about yours.
MID_EV14_005_m01_020: Though, to be honest, I think I've already surmised\na fair bit about the two of you.
MID_EV14_005_m01_021: For example, the way Buccar carries himself tells me\nhe's a soldier, through and through.
MID_EV14_005_m01_022: And based on your bearing, I'd wager you've even\nserved in the capital?
MID_EV14_005_m01_023: Oh?
MID_EV14_005_m01_024: You may not say much, but the habits ingrained in\nyou from years of service say more than enough.
MID_EV14_005_m01_025: But what of you, Miss Leda? Buccar serves you like\na retainer, does he not?
MID_EV14_005_m01_026: You are of some social standing, that much\nis obvious.
MID_EV14_005_m01_027: And that Bjor fellow seemed to know exactly who\nBuccar was. Or did you think I hadn't noticed?
MID_EV14_005_m01_028: I'd say there's no doubt you two were close to the\nviceroy during the days of Old Cydonia.
MID_EV14_005_m01_029: Mm.
MID_EV14_005_m01_030: I hate to bring your little guessing game to a close,\nbut I don't trust you.
MID_EV14_005_m01_031: Your identity is as unclear as ours, don't you\nthink, Sirocco?
MID_EV14_005_m01_032: You pretend to be so very carefree, and yet you're as\nguarded as any of us. A simple bard—I don't think so.
MID_EV14_005_m01_033: We both have secrets to keep, then. So be it. Let's\nconsider the topic closed for now.
MID_EV14_005_m01_034: There will be plenty of time for revelations during\nthe long journey ahead.
MID_EV14_006_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_006_m01_001: Morgan, Mace, Newman—all dead. And now\nBjor too?
MID_EV14_006_m01_002: Everyone involved in that siege has gone and got\nthemselves murdered. What a mess.
MID_EV14_006_m01_003: According to witnesses at the tavern, a young woman\nis responsible for the latest...mess.
MID_EV14_006_m01_004: Why, I imagine she'll be coming for you next.
MID_EV14_006_m01_005: Ohhh... The shadow of death approaches—I can\nhear the footsteps! Rrgh... How could this happen?!
MID_EV14_006_m01_006: Who leaked the information? Who would dare\nbetray me?!
MID_EV14_006_m01_007: I was just looking into that very thing.
MID_EV14_006_m01_008: How can you be so calm about this?! I bet you'd\nlook into it a little harder if YOU were the target!
MID_EV14_006_m01_009: What did you just say to me?
MID_EV14_006_m01_010: Oh, hey, I'm sorry. Please...I was joking—I didn't\nmean any disrespect.
MID_EV14_006_m01_011: Listen. There's a saying... "A miracle fallen from the\nheavens cannot match a mastery of the earth."
MID_EV14_006_m01_012: I don't...understand what that means.
MID_EV14_006_m01_013: It means that if you keep waiting on scraps to fall\nfrom above, you'll miss the bounty at your feet.
MID_EV14_006_m01_014: Where are we right now, Balboa? Is this not your\nvery own stronghold?
MID_EV14_006_m01_015: All you have to do is hide at the bottom of the mine,\nset a trap, and wait for the enemy to come to you.
MID_EV14_006_m01_016: I suppose you're right. This place is practically my\nown castle. I'll get started working on that trap.
MID_EV14_006_m01_017: I nearly forgot. Magistra Raksha gave me something\nfor you.
MID_EV14_006_m01_018: Ohhh! Is...is this...
MID_EV14_006_m01_019: It's one of Drake's treasures. You've heard of\nthem, surely.
MID_EV14_006_m01_020: Yeah, I've heard of them. They're supposed to be\nmagic and outlandishly powerful.
MID_EV14_006_m01_021: I heard that one of those treasures gave a single\npirate the power to conquer the entire Danann Sea.
MID_EV14_006_m01_022: Incredible! Even just holding it, I can feel the\nsurge of power! It's immense!
MID_EV14_006_m01_023: Are you sure about this? You trust...me...to use\nit properly?
MID_EV14_006_m01_024: Rest assured, the organization is well aware of your\npast contributions.
MID_EV14_006_m01_025: And if I'm being honest, we simply cannot afford to\nlose you here.
MID_EV14_006_m01_026: You see, we will spare no expense to support you.\nSo you can let those pesky doubts just...float away.
MID_EV14_006_m01_027: Hehehe... AHAHA! Looks like I have nothing to fear,\nthen! Come and get me if you dare!
MID_EV14_007_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_007_m01_001: Ahh, this ore... I'd wager I know exactly what it is.
MID_EV14_007_m01_002: <NCA>Ask what he's talking about.
MID_EV14_007_m01_003: <NCB>Ask if it's gold.
MID_EV14_007_m01_004: <ACA>All this mumbling about pretty rocks. Are they really\nso interesting?
MID_EV14_007_m01_005: <ACA>They are indeed. This is orichalcum—a rare metal\ntraded at a higher price than gold.
MID_EV14_007_m01_006: <ACA>I thought this was just a wasteland. I never expected\nto find something so precious here.
MID_EV14_007_m01_007: <ACB>Isn't this just...gold?
MID_EV14_007_m01_008: <ACB>It is not. In fact, it's far more valuable than that.
MID_EV14_007_m01_009: <ACB>No—it can't be. This is orichalcum? Something so\nvaluable...here?
MID_EV14_007_m01_010: What is this orichalcum stuff anyway?
MID_EV14_007_m01_011: It's called "deiform gold"—harder and tougher than\niron and capable of storing magic as well.
MID_EV14_007_m01_012: In fact, it's a divinium like adamantine. It's vital in\nthe production of powerful weapons such as Arcs.
MID_EV14_007_m01_013: I didn't know there was a metal harder than iron.
MID_EV14_007_m01_014: Yes, and orichalcum is an especially important\nresource for the temples.
MID_EV14_007_m01_015: No person or party—save those affiliated with the\ntemples—is allowed to possess large quantities of it.
MID_EV14_007_m01_016: See, if anyone had this ore in quantity, they'd have\nthe power to upend the temples and the empire itself.
MID_EV14_007_m01_017: For that reason, temple officials are supposed to\nclosely monitor the mining of this precious material.
MID_EV14_007_m01_018: I'm certain the workers here have been led to\nbelieve they're mining gold.
MID_EV14_007_m01_019: And I'm certain temple officials have no idea\norichalcum has been found here.
MID_EV14_007_m01_020: <NCA>Ask what it means.
MID_EV14_007_m01_021: <NCB>Dismiss the matter.
MID_EV14_007_m01_022: <ACA>The ore, the temples... What does all of this mean?
MID_EV14_007_m01_023: <ACA>It's difficult to liquidate orichalcum without arousing\ntemple suspicion.
MID_EV14_007_m01_024: <ACA>Processing even a small amount would catch their\neye, much less pulling a large volume from a mine.
MID_EV14_007_m01_025: <ACA>Someone like Balboa could never move a high-stakes\ncommodity like this.
MID_EV14_007_m01_026: <ACA>You ask what it means... It means Balboa has a\npowerful patron supporting her behind the scenes.
MID_EV14_007_m01_027: <ACB>Even so, none of this has anything to do with us.
MID_EV14_007_m01_028: <ACB>The only thing that matters about this place—\nwhatever it is—is that this is where I kill Balboa.
MID_EV14_007_m01_029: <ACB>Truly? You mean to tell me you don't wonder what\nand who is at work behind the curtain here?
MID_EV14_007_m01_030: Ah!
MID_EV14_007_m01_031: HAH hah hah! This whole trap business\nactually worked.
MID_EV14_007_m01_032: Hey, is this some kind of joke? You're the one who's\nbeen hunting us?! I heard it was a young woman...
MID_EV14_007_m01_033: but you're just a little girl. I can't believe the others\ngot taken out by a puny thing like you.
MID_EV14_007_m01_034: Balboa! Where is my mother?! She's supposed to be\nworking in this stupid mine of yours.
MID_EV14_007_m01_035: Her name is Mikaela, and she has to be here!
MID_EV14_007_m01_036: Mikaela's your mother? That witch went on a\nrampage and then escaped.
MID_EV14_007_m01_037: What? She just left?!
MID_EV14_007_m01_038: Why would she leave without finishing the job? She\nshould've captured you while she had the chance.
MID_EV14_007_m01_039: Is that what you're truly worried about, Mu?
MID_EV14_007_m01_040: Well, I wouldn't go planning any reunions if I were\nyou. You're all going to die right here...right now.
MID_EV14_007_m01_041: Do you think so, General Balboa? Balboa Beauclerc.\nThat's your name, right?
MID_EV14_007_m01_042: As commander of the Arges, Fourth Division of\nArago, you authorized the invasion of Cydonia.
MID_EV14_007_m01_043: You're the one responsible for what happened there.\nAnd don't you dare deny it.
MID_EV14_007_m01_044: You helped ruin my father's reputation, and you\ndestroyed lives...so many lives.
MID_EV14_007_m01_045: But you didn't stop, not even after you'd won. No,\nyou had your soldiers pillage the city relentlessly.
MID_EV14_007_m01_046: And what they took from those poor people went\nright into your pockets. That's what it says here.
MID_EV14_007_m01_047: "Father"? I see! You're his poor little daughter, aren't\nyou? Honestly, I had no idea you were still alive.
MID_EV14_007_m01_048: Where did you get this information, anyway?
MID_EV14_007_m01_049: Who betrayed us?! Tell me now!
MID_EV14_007_m01_050: I can't imagine why it matters to someone who's\nabout to die.
MID_EV14_007_m01_051: You think it's going to be that easy, huh? You might\nthink again, because I have one of Drake's treasures.
MID_EV14_007_m01_052: Drake's treasures?! If she's telling the truth, then\nshe has a thing of legend in her possession.
MID_EV14_007_m01_053: If the rumors about them are true, things could get\nvery ugly. Careful, Miss Leda!
MID_EV14_007_m01_054: I hear Obsidian...crying.
MID_EV14_007_m01_055: That thing she's holding is...resonating...with\nObsidian somehow. But why?
MID_EV14_008_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_008_m01_001: Wait, please... You win. I give up. Please, please,\nlet me live.
MID_EV14_008_m01_002: Mu, it's time for you to step away for a bit. Adults\nonly for a little while.
MID_EV14_008_m01_003: Oh...yeah, OK.
MID_EV14_008_m01_004: Will you be alright on your own? I can come with\nyou, if you want.
MID_EV14_008_m01_005: Stop treating me like a child! I'll be fine!
MID_EV14_008_m01_006: *sigh* When will she understand that these tantrums\nare exactly why we treat her like a child.
MID_EV14_008_m01_007: Balboa, you know where Lechner is, don't you?
MID_EV14_008_m01_008: If I tell you where he is, he'll kill me. So, I'm dead\neither way.
MID_EV14_008_m01_009: I see. That's fine. I'll find him myself.
MID_EV14_008_m01_010: S-stop... Please...
MID_EV14_008_m01_011: I'm tired of the sound of your voice. Apologize to\neveryone you killed when you get to the underworld.
MID_EV14_008_m01_012: <NCA>Kill Balboa.
MID_EV14_008_m01_034: 
MID_EV14_008_m01_013: Aaaaagh!
MID_EV14_008_m01_014: Urk...hng... Damn that...vixen.
MID_EV14_008_m01_015: How dare she...throw me to the wolves...
MID_EV14_008_m01_016: "Vixen"?
MID_EV14_008_m01_017: Miss Leda, I didn't say anything when you\ndispatched Bjor...
MID_EV14_008_m01_018: And I know there was no saving Balboa with those\ninjuries of hers... But still, did you need to go so far?
MID_EV14_008_m01_019: You didn't put her out of her misery. You executed\nboth of them with far more brutality than necessary.
MID_EV14_008_m01_020: It was necessary. They're monsters. I can't just...kill\nthem. I have to make them regret what they've done.
MID_EV14_008_m01_021: The only way to do that is to fill their last moments\nwith fear and despair.
MID_EV14_008_m01_022: It wouldn't count as revenge otherwise.
MID_EV14_008_m01_023: And with that, Balboa is gone. Only one name\nremains: Lechner.
MID_EV14_008_m01_024: Your vengeance is nearly complete.
MID_EV14_008_m01_025: Is it? I'm curious about the "vixen" Balboa\nmentioned in her last breath.
MID_EV14_008_m01_026: Miss Leda, if I may... What do you know about\nthis Lechner?
MID_EV14_008_m01_027: I know that his work was the catalyst that set the\nCydonia Massacre in motion.
MID_EV14_008_m01_028: But I don't know anything more than that, and I've\nnever met him.
MID_EV14_008_m01_029: You plan to take revenge on a person you've never\nmet before?
MID_EV14_008_m01_030: I do. I won't be leaving any of the people named on\nthis list alive.
MID_EV14_008_m01_031: I don't care where he's hiding. I'll scour this land\nuntil I find him and kill him with my own hands.
MID_EV14_008_m01_032: I will not fail, and I will make no exceptions.
MID_EV14_008_m01_033: Ah...
MID_EV14_009_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_009_m01_001: Milady, we freed everyone trapped in the mine.
MID_EV14_009_m01_002: I admit that thunderous voice of yours did come in\nhandy, Buccar. It helped guide many to safety.
MID_EV14_009_m01_003: I expect news of Balboa's death will have spread\nthrough town by now.
MID_EV14_009_m01_004: Why isn't Mu with you?
MID_EV14_009_m01_005: She went to town to see if she could learn anything\nabout her mother's whereabouts.
MID_EV14_009_m01_006: Why, Miss Leda... Have you taken a shine to Mu?
MID_EV14_009_m01_007: Perhaps she reminds you of yourself when you\nwere her age?
MID_EV14_009_m01_008: Please...it's not like that.
MID_EV14_009_m01_009: How did it go, Mu? Did you get the information\nyou were hoping for?
MID_EV14_009_m01_010: Yeah, I talked to some of the prisoners who knew\nmy mother.
MID_EV14_009_m01_011: It's like Balboa said––she escaped.
MID_EV14_009_m01_012: And I guess everyone Balboa sent after her...ended\nup dead.
MID_EV14_009_m01_013: It sounds like your mother is quite resourceful...and\nperhaps a bit terrifying. I must ask—who is she?
MID_EV14_009_m01_014: She used to be a mercenary, but she said she retired\nwhen I was born.
MID_EV14_009_m01_015: She told me her nickname was Mikaela Redblade.\nI guess she was pretty famous?
MID_EV14_009_m01_016: I've heard that name before! I never would've\nguessed that was your mother!
MID_EV14_009_m01_017: What?! So then, what she said was true? She really\nwas famous?
MID_EV14_009_m01_018: But Mu, did you find out where your mother went?
MID_EV14_009_m01_019: She told the other miners she was going to try\nto find somewhere to make good money.
MID_EV14_009_m01_020: A place to make money? She might have headed to\nDagsion or thereabouts.
MID_EV14_009_m01_021: Ah?
MID_EV14_009_m01_022: Oh no! Look, up on the hill! Balboa's mansion\nis burning!
MID_EV14_009_m01_023: So it is. It looks like the good citizens of the town\nhave surrounded the place.
MID_EV14_009_m01_024: After living under Balboa's boot for so long, I imagine\nthey won't be showing much restraint.
MID_EV14_009_m01_025: They probably looted the mansion before setting\nit on fire.
MID_EV14_009_m01_026: I'm sure they harbor many grudges—some even from\nthe Cydonia Massacre—but this is not right.
MID_EV14_009_m01_027: No, it's not. They've likely killed the mansion guards.\nWorse yet, Balboa's family must be inside.
MID_EV14_009_m01_028: Her parents, husband...their children... What will\nthe townspeople do to them?
MID_EV14_009_m01_029: By the look of things, her kin will either burn to\ndeath in the mansion or die as soon as they escape.
MID_EV14_009_m01_030: How could the people do that?! Balboa was horrible,\nbut this is just...
MID_EV14_009_m01_031: She was a cruel viceroy, to be sure. But perhaps in\nher children's eyes she was a good mother.
MID_EV14_009_m01_032: Ah, but such things are irrelevant to the townsfolk\nnow. They're full of too much grief and anger to care.
MID_EV14_009_m01_033: Ah...
MID_EV14_009_m01_034: Miss Leda, is this what you want from revenge? Does\nkilling the ones you hate truly ease your suffering?
MID_EV14_009_m01_035: I will kill the people on my list. If there's collateral\ndamage, so be it.
MID_EV14_009_m01_036: *sigh* What an appalling thing to say. Do you\nreally mean that?
MID_EV14_009_m01_037: Stop talking. I've had enough of you.
MID_EV14_009_m01_038: Milady...
MID_EV14_009_m01_039: But the people of Kassite can bring peace to their\ntown now, right?
MID_EV14_009_m01_040: I wish I could say that was true, but that's not going\nto happen.
MID_EV14_009_m01_041: Soon the kingdom of Arago will appoint a new\nviceroy to take Balboa's place.
MID_EV14_009_m01_042: That viceroy is sure to retaliate for this raid. And\njust like that, the people will be under the boot again.
MID_EV14_009_m01_043: No...
MID_EV14_009_m01_044: Whether it is big events or small ones, history seems\nbound to repeat itself.